## What changed

**`lib/idempotency.ts`** (new) — `newIdempotencyKey()`, a plain module (no `server-only`) so the client can call it. UUID v4 via `crypto.randomUUID()`, with a `getRandomValues`/`Math.random` fallback because `randomUUID` only exists in a secure context and a POS served over http on a LAN IP is exactly the deployment where a double charge matters.

**`app/sell/page.tsx`** — `Ticket` gains `idempotencyKey`, generated in `makeTicket()`. `handleConfirm` reads it from the active ticket and passes it to `createSale`. The key is rotated **only** when the sale registers (alongside `cart: []` / `lastSaleId`); if the call fails, the key survives and the retry resends it. Each ticket tab has its own.

**`lib/actions.ts`** — `createSale(items, idempotencyKey)`. The parameter is required, not optional, so `tsc` flags any caller that forgets it. Sent as `headers: { "Idempotency-Key": key }`. A blank key is dropped rather than forwarded: the service stores `""` verbatim and its unique `(location_id, idempotency_key)` would make every keyless sale in a store collide with the others.

**`lib/inventoryClient.ts`** — `apiFetch` now merges caller headers *before* its own. Previously they spread last, so a caller could overwrite `Authorization`; now it can add but not replace.

## Tests

`app/sell/page.test.tsx` (new, jsdom + Testing Library — the repo's first component test) covers the AC directly: retry of the same ticket sends the same key, the key rotates after the sale registers, and each tab gets its own. I verified it the other way round — swapping `activeTicket.idempotencyKey` for `newIdempotencyKey()` inside `handleConfirm` fails two of the three. Plus `lib/idempotency.test.ts` (format, uniqueness, both fallback branches), two cases in `lib/actions.test.ts` (header forwarded, blank key omitted), and two in `lib/inventoryClient.test.ts` (header merge, credential not overridable).

`npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test` (119 tests, 12 files) and `npm run build` all pass. No new user-visible strings, so no i18n change.

One thing I did not do: verify against the running inventory service. The contract was confirmed by reading `inventory-service/src/app/v1/sales/route.ts:43` (`req.headers.get("idempotency-key")`) and `src/lib/inventory/sales.ts` (replay lookup inside the transaction, plus a unique-violation rescue). Learnings appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`, including two new entries in `## Codebase Patterns`. No commits made.

